  "result": "```js\nasync function getUser(id) {\n  const rows = await db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [id]);\n  if (!rows.length) throw new Error('Not found');\n  return rows[0];\n}\n```\n\nKey changes:\n- `async` function replaces the `callback` parameter\n- `await` replaces the callback passed to `db.query`\n- Errors propagate via `throw` / rejected promise instead of `callback(err)`\n- The result is returned directly instead of passed to `callback(null, result)`\n\nCallers swap from `getUser(id, (err, user) => ...)` to `const user = await getUser(id)` (inside an `async` function), or chain `.catch()` for error handling.\n\n> **Note:** This assumes `db.query` already returns a promise. If it's callback-only, wrap it first with `util.promisify(db.query.bind(db))` or a manual `new Promise(...)` wrapper.",
